# Stage1 semantic — the `DiagnosticKind` enum (`extend Semantic: public:`): one ordinal
# per diagnostic stage1 can report, matching stage0's set.
#
# The wording and severity for each kind live in diagnostic_messages/ and
# semantic_api_severity.elisa — a new kind must be given both.

extend Semantic:
    public:
        # The category of a diagnostic. Human-readable wording and LSP severity for each
        # kind are the frontend's responsibility — see `diagnostic_message` /
        # `diagnostic_severity` in semantic_api. Consumers (LSP, CLI) render those rather
        # than re-deriving text/severity per kind. Both the parser (syntax findings) and
        # the checker (semantic findings) feed the one `SymbolTable.diagnostics` stream, so
        # this enum spans both — `Semantic::check` folds `Ast::File.errors` in via
        # `parse_error_kind`.
        const enum DiagnosticKind of u16:
include "./diagnostic_kind_frontend.elisa"
include "./diagnostic_kind_type_flow.elisa"
include "./diagnostic_kind_effects_regions.elisa"
